EXPLICIT METRIC / OBSERVABILITY
Positive assertion is an ABSOLUTE strict current sampled RSS <268435456 bytes
for one dedicated fresh consumer PROCESS using the unchanged v2 core.
It is not an allocation delta, a thread metric, a process.resourceUsage lifetime
high-water, or a whole-verifier/process-tree RSS bound. No baseline subtraction,
threshold increase, forced GC, hidden retry or historical failure waiver.
The independent consumer is freshly spawned before any tree/materializer/prefix
controls. Its module imports, observer, PIN parsing, hashing and consumption
all count toward its current RSS. Earliest baseline means after observer imports,
not OS-exec startup. New full telemetry does NOT subtract this setup baseline.
Native core samples at stream entry/every256 chunks/successful final hash.
Additional consumer samples occur at baseline, before-stream, first-consume,
every256 chunks, blocked timeout, each mutant allocation and stream settlement.
Both the native positive maximum AND observed consumer fieldwise RSS peak must
satisfy the unchanged strict threshold. Samples cannot bound unobserved peaks.
Producer is a different process and is accounted separately without an invented
256MiB assertion. Supervisor memory is recorded separately and explicitly NOT
waived as a total-verifier claim: no total-verifier bound is tested here.
All five memory fields are bytes: rss, heapUsed, heapTotal, external, arrayBuffers.
Fieldwise maxima are not necessarily simultaneous. No host-load isolation claim.

Positive uses real 1,073,872,896 bytes (1GiB+128KiB) of 0x61, generated in
16,386 writes of65,536 bytes, same SHA256 as v2 in PIN.json. Transport may split
or coalesce raw fragments, so observed consumer chunk count is recorded, not
falsely equated to producer write count. Core slices at65,536 and rejects raw
fragments above1,048,576. Awaited consumer pending/bytes are independently counted;
incremental observer hash retains no chunks. No main-process allocation stress.
Producer preload forwards stdout.write with original receiver/arguments/return;
records accepted bytes/writes, false writes/drain events, writableLength samples
and writableHighWaterMark. It preserves the producer buffer/data/drain loop.
Sampled queue lengths are Node observations, not kernel occupancy or absolute
queue bounds. Consumer pendingBytes is callback-owned bytes, not readableLength.
On SIGTERM only, preload durably writes a final producer receipt then re-raises
SIGTERM; this disclosed telemetry lifecycle addition leaves normal fixture bytes
and natural exit behavior unchanged. Core still owns producer kill/wait/close.

FINITE DECLARED RECIPE — EXACTLY ONE ATTEMPT EACH, IN ORDER
1 positive: fresh consumer/producer, full unchanged over1GiB data/digest, genuine
  slow awaited consumer via setImmediate; both natural status0, no forced kill.
2 producer-exit7: same full data/digest, original producer's existing exit7 arg;
  core STREAM_PROCESS must reach coordinator as worker exit17, not an import or
  parse failure; producer must have naturally exited7 and no live process remains.
3 consumer-failure: callback throws V3_CONSUMER_FAILURE after16 real chunks;
  core must terminate/reap active producer, worker must forward exact failure and
  naturally exit17; coordinator records operationSucceeded=false, not product pass.
4 timeout: callback blocks after16 real chunks, sends timeout-ready; parent timer
  after250ms sends V3_TIMEOUT, releases callback with that exact error, core reaps
  producer, worker persists receipt and naturally exits17. This is intentional
  cooperative cancellation, NOT a positive product outcome or assertion-only test.
5 allocation-mutant: ONLY dedicated consumer allocates/touches/retains8MiB of0x5a
  per callback, in addition to real stream consumption. Each allocation is sampled,
  fsynced and IPC-handshaken before the next allocation. Parent detects sampled
  RSS >=268435456, fsyncs RESOURCE-BOUNDARY, stops further allocations, sends
  V3_RSS_LIMIT. Core kills/reaps producer; worker durably records complete failure
  receipt and remains alive retaining allocations. Parent persists BEFORE-KILL,
  then really sends consumer SIGTERM and awaits close. SIGTERM death is REQUIRED;
  an assertion-only rejection is insufficient. This is an intentionally killed
  harness-mutant, NOT a natural positive product result.

Mutant bounded envelope: at most40 allocations =335544320 retained bytes,45s
whole-control deadline,3s cooperative cleanup grace then emergency SIGTERM and
3s escalation to SIGKILL. Expected sampled RSS overshoot must be <67108864 bytes
above boundary. No next8MiB allocation is admitted after observed crossing.
This is stepwise supervised detection, not an OS continuous hard-RSS guarantee;
incidental native overhead/unobserved peaks are not bounded by the8MiB step.
Failure to reach boundary before allocation cap, oversized measured overshoot,
emergency fallback, missing receipt, parse/import errors, unexpected statuses,
live/zombie producer/consumer or group members all FAIL the control. No relabeling.
All controls have45s deadlines and emergency process-group cleanup. Parent records
error/close, all messages and signals; waits direct child close; checks group via
pinned ps and consumer/producer PID absence via signal0. Normal receipt implies
core awaited producer close. Any post-close orphan requires kill and a failed
control. Producer SIGTERM and consumer SIGTERM are distinguished in raw receipts.
Arbitrary supervisor SIGKILL, OS failure or disk failure cannot guarantee durable
final telemetry; missing fields are failures, never invented numbers or passes.

RECEIPTS / FAILURE POLICY
Fresh unique output directory; writes are exclusive. Baseline/samples, producer
start/final receipt, consumer final receipt, parent RAW-RECEIPT and mutation
boundary/before-kill events are persisted BEFORE coordinator assertions. Journals
and JSON receipts fsync before returning. Assertions write a separate VERDICT;
failure cannot discard already persisted numeric/status evidence. Consumer errors
retain observed bytes/chunks/hash and memory even when native core returns no
metrics. Supervisor RAW-RECEIPT records missing/corrupt child artifacts explicitly.
operationSucceeded=false on every deliberate negative; expected-control-outcome
only says the control detected the intended boundary. No negative is a product pass.
Unexpected failure stops the remaining recipe; no fix/reexecution until root review.
Postflight and evidence sealing still occur, even when the recipe is not green.

